# Linker & Build Conventions

## Cross-Compiler Toolchain
- **Bootloader (stage1/stage2/loader)**: `i686-elf-gcc`, `i686-elf-ld`, `nasm`
- **Kernel**: `i686-elf-gcc` (currently 32-bit despite `arch/x86_64/` path — do NOT use `-m64` until explicitly migrated)
- **Userland**: `i686-elf-gcc` with `-m32`; never use host `gcc` for target code
- Always verify toolchain with `scripts/check-toolchain.sh` before building

## Compiler Flags

### Kernel flags (all kernel C/C++ files)
```
-ffreestanding -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions -fno-stack-protector
-nostdlib -nostdinc -Wall -Wextra -O2 -m32 -std=c++17
```

### Bootloader stage2 C++ flags
```
-ffreestanding -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions -fno-stack-protector
-nostdlib -m32 -std=c++17
-I bootloader/include
```

### Userland flags
```
-m32 -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -O2
-I userland/libc/include
```
- Userland is NOT `-ffreestanding`; it links against `userland/libc/libc.a` and `userland/libc/crt/crt0.o`

## Linker Scripts
- **Kernel linker script**: `kernel/arch/x86_64/boot/linker.ld`
  - Kernel loads at physical `0x100000` (1MB)
  - Sections order: `.multiboot`, `.text`, `.rodata`, `.data`, `.bss`
  - Entry symbol: `kernel_entry` (defined in `entry.asm`)
- **Bootloader**: No linker script for stage1/stage2 (flat binary via `nasm -f bin`)
- **Loader**: `bootloader/src/loader/Makefile` produces flat binary at `0x10000`

```ld
/* ✅ GOOD - kernel linker.ld skeleton */
ENTRY(kernel_entry)
SECTIONS {
    . = 0x100000;
    .multiboot : { *(.multiboot) }
    .text      : { *(.text*) }
    .rodata    : { *(.rodata*) }
    .data      : { *(.data*) }
    .bss       : { *(COMMON) *(.bss*) }
}
```

## Disk Image Layout
The disk image (`bootloader/build/disk.img`) is assembled with `dd`:

| Offset (sectors) | Content         | Size      | Load Address |
|------------------|-----------------|-----------|--------------|
| 0                | stage1.bin      | 512 B     | 0x7C00       |
| 1                | stage2.bin      | 9 sectors | 0x7E00       |
| 10               | loader.bin      | variable  | 0x10000      |
| after loader     | kernel.bin (ELF)| variable  | 0x100000     |

- Sector counts and offsets **must stay in sync** between `bootloader/Makefile`, `common/constants.inc`, and `bootloader/include/boot.hpp`
- `SECTOR_SIZE = 512` — never hardcode 512 inline; use the constant
- Use `dd if=/dev/zero` to pad gaps; never leave uninitialized bytes between sections

## Makefile Patterns
- Top-level `Makefile` calls sub-makes: `make -C bootloader all` then `make -C kernel all`
- Each subdirectory has its own `Makefile`; never glob-compile (`*.cpp`) — list sources explicitly
- Object files go in `build/` subdirectory relative to the Makefile, not alongside sources
- Use `$(MAKE)` not `make` for recursive calls
- Add `.PHONY: all clean` to every Makefile

```makefile
# ✅ GOOD - minimal kernel Makefile pattern
CC      := i686-elf-gcc
CXX     := i686-elf-g++
CXXFLAGS := -ffreestanding -fno-rtti -fno-exceptions -m32 -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra

SRCS := kernel.cpp panic.cpp printk.cpp
OBJS := $(SRCS:%.cpp=build/%.o)

all: build/kernel.bin

build/%.o: %.cpp | build
	$(CXX) $(CXXFLAGS) -c $< -o $@

build:
	mkdir -p build

.PHONY: all clean
```

## NASM Output Formats
- Stage1 / Stage2 / Loader: `nasm -f bin` → flat binary
- Assembly files that link with C++ objects: `nasm -f elf32`
- Never mix `elf64` objects with `-m32` C++ objects

## Post-change verification

After substantive edits, run the **clean rebuild + QEMU** sequence in `.cursor/rules/verify-build.mdc` (from repo root: clean `kernel/build` and `bootloader/build`, then `make -C kernel`, `make -C bootloader all`, `make -C bootloader run`).

